{"parentUuid":"a17d591e-5064-4425-a9ed-b67b8f2f1479","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a55aa02cbc6f623ac","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Ew3yPfMx523199KuvPJ4wy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CZqVQ8zKbneeX9fcK5pV4E","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"Large Language Models as Optimizers\" Yang DeepMind OPRO paper"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8131,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":336,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8131},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":336,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8131,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosMdbz5K1GhvcfQPL59","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c1819519-528b-44df-8496-93fe0e4d2336","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:49.998Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"182fe87e-ecdd-42ef-a62b-485d5fcd8f2b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a55aa02cbc6f623ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0151tzumwphQZRxP7gQASUsM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"In-context learning combinatorial optimization LLM survey 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"LARGE LANGUAGE MODELS FOR COMBINATORIAL OPTIMIZATION: A SYSTEMATIC REVIEW\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.03637\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ai4co/awesome-fm4co: Recent research papers about Foundation Models for Combinatorial Optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ai4co/awesome-fm4co\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"A survey on large language models driven meta-optimizers for automated intelligent optimization | Artificial Intelligence Review | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10462-025-11470-w\"},{\"title\":\"Discovering heuristics with Large Language Models (LLMs) for mixed-integer programs: Single-machine scheduling - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054825003545\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS Poster Large Language Models as End-to-end Combinatorial Optimization Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/115835\"},{\"title\":\"A Systematic Survey on Large Language Models for Algorithm Design\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2410.14716v5\"},{\"title\":\"Large Language Models for Combinatorial Optimization: A Systematic Review | ACM Computing Surveys\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3801961\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - FeiLiu36/LLM4AlgorithmDesign: A Collection on Large Language Models for Optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/FeiLiu36/LLM4Opt\"},{\"title\":\"Infeasibility Aware Large Language Models for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.01455v1\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive search results related to in-context learning, combinatorial optimization, and large language models. Here's a summary of the key findings:\n\n## Recent Surveys and Reviews (2025-2026)\n\nA systematic review aims to consolidate the current state-of-the-art in LLMs applied to combinatorial optimization, with a citation tracking performed on January 13, 2025.\n\nLarge Language Models have notably enhanced automation and innovation in algorithm design, yielding remarkable progress in areas ranging from combinatorial optimization to scientific discovery.\n\nA systematic review explores the application of LLMs in combinatorial optimization, examining over 2,000 publications and selecting 103 studies.\n\n## Applications of LLMs in Combinatorial Optimization\n\nResearch shows three main paradigms:\n\n1. **Solver Component Generation**: LLMs generate reusable solver components, such as heuristics, search operators, or executable code\n\n2. **Auto-Formulation**: LLMs serve as auto-formulation engines that translate natural-language descriptions into mathematical models, solver code, or optimization pipelines\n\n3. **End-to-End Solvers**: A novel framework empowers LLMs to serve as end-to-end CO solvers by directly mapping natural language problem descriptions to solutions, using supervised fine-tuning and reinforcement learning\n\n## In-Context Learning Capabilities\n\nInitial efforts to utilize LLMs as optimizers leverage the in-context learning capabilities of LLMs to generate new solutions for specific problems based on previously evaluated solutions.\n\nThe search results show an active and growing field with multiple recent surveys and significant research developments in 2025-2026.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6066e25e-5a72-4285-8bff-718124e092ab","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:55.477Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"182fe87e-ecdd-42ef-a62b-485d5fcd8f2b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a139ab1e-971c-419a-bcbb-84e5da9f109e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a55aa02cbc6f623ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ASnES7LsRLzDMRKsMvDqz6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OpenAI o1 o3 SAT CSP combinatorial optimization benchmark 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OpenAI o1 - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI_o1\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI o3 Released: Benchmarks and Comparison to o1\",\"url\":\"https://www.helicone.ai/blog/openai-o3\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI’s O3: Features, O1 Comparison, Benchmarks & More | DataCamp\",\"url\":\"https://www.datacamp.com/blog/o3-openai\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI o3 Benchmark Results: AIME, GPQA & SWE-bench\",\"url\":\"https://aibusinessweekly.net/p/openai-o3-benchmarks\"},{\"title\":\"OPT-Engine: Benchmarking the Limits of LLMs in Optimization Modeling via Complexity Scaling\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2601.19924\"},{\"title\":\"Open AI's O3 Benchmarking: Redefining Standards in AI Performance\",\"url\":\"https://www.gocodeo.com/post/open-ais-o3-benchmarking\"},{\"title\":\"Unveiling OpenAI o3: From benchmarks to real world | Our Insights | Plante Moran\",\"url\":\"https://www.plantemoran.com/explore-our-thinking/insight/2025/01/unveiling-openai-o3-from-benchmarks-to-real-world\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI o3: Release Date, Features and Model Comparison\",\"url\":\"https://www.analyticsvidhya.com/blog/2025/01/openai-o3-vs-competitors-performance-and-applications/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI releases o3, a model that tops 99% of human competitors on IOI 2024 and Codeforces benchmarks - Research & Development World\",\"url\":\"https://www.rdworldonline.com/openai-releases-o3-a-model-that-tops-99-of-human-competitors-on-ioi-2024-and-codeforces-benchmarks/\"},{\"title\":\"Technical Performance | The 2025 AI Index Report\",\"url\":\"https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2025-ai-index-report/technical-performance\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding OpenAI's o1 and o3 models and their performance on various benchmarks:\n\n## OpenAI o1 and o3 Overview\n\nOpenAI shared in December 2024 benchmark results for its successor, o3 (the name o2 was skipped to avoid trademark conflict with the mobile carrier brand named O2).\n\n## Benchmark Performance\n\nOpenAI o3's key benchmark scores are: AIME 2024 math - 96.7%; GPQA Diamond PhD science - 87.7%; SWE-bench Verified software engineering - 71.7%; ARC-AGI-1 general reasoning - 87.5% at high compute; Codeforces competitive programming - 2,727 Elo; FrontierMath research-level math - 25.2%; MMLU general knowledge - 91.6%; HumanEval coding - 81.3%.\n\nNotably, on FrontierMath, which tests unseen research-level problems, o3 scored 25.2% - approximately 12x better than any previous model.\n\n## Combinatorial Optimization Context\n\nThe search results reference research on LLMs and combinatorial optimization. The recent success of reasoning models, such as OpenAI's o1 and DeepSeek-R1, has revitalized purely text-based paradigms. However, the specific SAT/CSP combinatorial optimization benchmarks for o1/o3 are not directly detailed in these search results.\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about SAT and CSP benchmark results for these models?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e9b87f48-df46-46f1-8a3c-273769fef3bd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:55.838Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a139ab1e-971c-419a-bcbb-84e5da9f109e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c1819519-528b-44df-8496-93fe0e4d2336","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a55aa02cbc6f623ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CZqVQ8zKbneeX9fcK5pV4E","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Large Language Models as Optimizers\" Yang DeepMind OPRO paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2309.03409] Large Language Models as Optimizers\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.03409\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/opro: official code for \\\"Large Language Models as Optimizers\\\" · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/opro\"},{\"title\":\"LARGE LANGUAGE MODELS AS OPTIMIZERS Chengrun Yang* Xuezhi Wang Yifeng Lu\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2309.03409\"},{\"title\":\"Large Language Models as Optimizers | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=Bb4VGOWELI\"},{\"title\":\"Large Language Models as Optimizers\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2309.03409\"},{\"title\":\"Large Language Models As Optimizers – OPRO by Google DeepMind - AI Papers Academy\",\"url\":\"https://aipapersacademy.com/large-language-models-as-optimizers/\"},{\"title\":\"Paper page - Large Language Models as Optimizers\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2309.03409\"},{\"title\":\"opro/README.md at main · google-deepmind/opro\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/opro/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"DeepMind discovers that AI large language models can optimize their own prompts | VentureBeat\",\"url\":\"https://venturebeat.com/business/deepmind-discovers-that-ai-large-language-models-can-optimize-their-own-prompts\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind Researchers Propose Optimization by PROmpting (OPRO): Large Language Models as Optimizers - MarkTechPost\",\"url\":\"https://www.marktechpost.com/2023/09/12/google-deepmind-researchers-propose-optimization-by-prompting-opro-large-language-models-as-optimizers/\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive information about the OPRO paper. Here's a summary of the key findings:\n\n## Paper Overview\n\nThe paper proposes Optimization by PROmpting (OPRO), a simple and effective approach to leverage large language models (LLMs) as optimizers, where the optimization task is described in natural language.\n\n## How OPRO Works\n\nIn each optimization step, the LLM generates new solutions from the prompt that contains previously generated solutions with their values, then the new solutions are evaluated and added to the prompt for the next optimization step.\n\n## Applications and Results\n\nThe work showcases OPRO on linear regression and traveling salesman problems, then moves on to the main application in prompt optimization, where the goal is to find instructions that maximize task accuracy.\n\nThe results are impressive: With a variety of LLMs, the best prompts optimized by OPRO outperform human-designed prompts by up to 8% on GSM8K, and by up to 50% on Big-Bench Hard tasks.\n\n## Authors and Publication Details\n\nThe paper is authored by Chengrun Yang, Xuezhi Wang, Yifeng Lu, Hanxiao Liu, Quoc V. Le, Denny Zhou, and Xinyun Chen from Google DeepMind, with arXiv reference 2309.03409.\n\nThe official code is available on GitHub at https://github.com/google-deepmind/opro.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9ec31a57-edef-4cbc-b19c-dd72b4c90a1c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:56.317Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c1819519-528b-44df-8496-93fe0e4d2336","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a17d591e-5064-4425-a9ed-b67b8f2f1479","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a55aa02cbc6f623ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QAjQ5Hyu8E3p9vPeqXJ73J","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DeepSeek R1 reasoning model combinatorial optimization NP-hard\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"DeepSeek-R1: Incentivizing Reasoning Capability in LLMs via\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.12948\"},{\"title\":\"From Zero to Reasoning Hero: How DeepSeek-R1 Leverages Reinforcement Learning to Master Complex Reasoning\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/NormalUhr/deepseek-r1-explained\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek-R1: Incentivizing Reasoning Capability in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2501.12948v1\"},{\"title\":\"[2510.16476] NP-Engine: Empowering Optimization Reasoning in Large Language Models with Verifiable Synthetic NP Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.16476\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek-R1 incentivizes reasoning in LLMs through reinforcement learning | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09422-z\"},{\"title\":\"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1 · Hugging Face\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1 · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1\"},{\"title\":\"Aman's AI Journal • Primers • DeepSeek-R1\",\"url\":\"https://aman.ai/primers/ai/deepseek-R1/\"},{\"title\":\"[2501.12948] DeepSeek-R1: Incentivizing Reasoning Capability in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.12948\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek-R1 Overview: Features, Capabilities, Parameters\",\"url\":\"https://fireworks.ai/blog/deepseek-r1-deepdive\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about DeepSeek R1, reasoning models, and combinatorial optimization with NP-hard problems:\n\n## DeepSeek R1 Reasoning Model\n\nDeepSeek-R1 demonstrates that reasoning abilities of LLMs can be incentivized through pure reinforcement learning, with the RL framework facilitating emergent development of advanced reasoning patterns such as self-reflection, verification, and dynamic strategy adaptation. The model is built on DeepSeek-V3 Base using Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) as its RL framework, with the reward signal based only on the correctness of final predictions.\n\n## Combinatorial Optimization and NP-Hard Problems\n\nWhile DeepSeek R1 excels at verifiable reasoning tasks, research shows that models like DeepSeek R1 excel at mathematics, coding, logic, and puzzles through Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards, but their ability to solve more complex optimization problems—particularly NP-hard tasks—remains underexplored.\n\nTo address this gap, researchers propose NP-ENGINE, the first comprehensive framework for training and evaluating LLMs on NP-hard problems, which covers 10 tasks across five domains with a generator-verifier-heuristic pipeline enabling scalable and verifiable RLVR training.\n\n## Technical Challenges\n\nMonte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS) for hierarchical solution exploration faced combinatorial explosion in the generation space and a fragile value model, proving too unwieldy in the large-scale RL context used for DeepSeek-R1.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d5d72c6b-9cf7-4e81-836e-91ee758a4a04","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:56.847Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a17d591e-5064-4425-a9ed-b67b8f2f1479","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
