{"parentUuid":"d2235eb1-6676-46cf-ab75-fc453774236f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a55aa02cbc6f623ac","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01EViwUH9ucPnB8z31Zo37CW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BThcxxuzPjScvHKke2JW9K","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"LLM \"as optimizer\" small scale failure scaling combinatorial limitation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6624,"cache_read_input_tokens":37511,"output_tokens":199,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6624},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":199,"cache_read_input_tokens":37511,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6624,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6624,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosRXv3b1LqcwheTeZdA","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"fbd0fa43-762b-4a06-b996-3076c036ce6c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:41.621Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d2235eb1-6676-46cf-ab75-fc453774236f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a55aa02cbc6f623ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RtpHe3QKBK6L2FUxx1DoLZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"reasoning model\" 2D packing rectangle placement spatial reasoning failure\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FloorplanQA: A Benchmark for Spatial Reasoning in LLMs using Structured Representations\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.07644\"},{\"title\":\"Unfolding Spatial Cognition: Evaluating Multimodal Models on Visual Simulations\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.04633v1\"},{\"title\":\"Spatial Reasoning is Not a Free Lunch: A Controlled Study on LLaVA\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2603.12545\"},{\"title\":\"Transformer-based placement heuristic for online 2D strip packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360835225006102\"},{\"title\":\"Mitigating Dimensionality in 2D Rectangle Packing Problem under Reinforcement Learning Schema\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.09677v1\"},{\"title\":\"Spatial reasoning skills about 2D representations of 3D geometrical shapes in grades 4 to 9 | Mathematics Education Research Journal | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s13394-020-00335-w\"},{\"title\":\"Mitigating Dimensionality in 2D Rectangle Packing Problem under Reinforcement\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2409.09677\"},{\"title\":\"Why 3D spatial reasoning still trips up today’s AI systems - MBZUAI\",\"url\":\"https://mbzuai.ac.ae/news/why-3d-spatial-reasoning-still-trips-up-todays-ai-systems/\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Two-dimensional irregular packing problems: A review\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/mechanical-engineering/articles/10.3389/fmech.2022.966691/full\"},{\"title\":\"RoboSpatial: Teaching Spatial Understanding to 2D and 3D Vision-Language Models for Robotics\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2411.16537v1\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found several relevant research papers and insights about reasoning models and their failures in spatial tasks like 2D packing and rectangle placement:\n\n## Key Findings on Spatial Reasoning Failures\n\nTool-augmented models generate Python code with incorrect algorithms when dealing with rectangle placement—treating boundary contact as collision or performing incomplete search over rectangle orientations—indicating that the bottleneck for complex spatial tasks is algorithmic reasoning about spatial constraints, not numerical precision.\n\nModels find reasoning over simple 2D transformations relatively easy but struggle with 3D cube net folding and tangram puzzles, performing near random chance due to the need for multi-step simulations.\n\n## Vision-Language Model Limitations\n\nSpatial failures in vision-language models are strongly coupled to the visual backbone, as encoders optimized primarily for global image–text alignment do not reliably support spatial reasoning, while encoders trained with denser or generative objectives can improve spatial outcomes within the same multimodal framework.\n\n## Broader Spatial Understanding Issues\n\nDespite significant recent advancements, vision-language models still fall short in spatial understanding and struggle with tasks that require interpreting nuanced spatial relationships between objects, such as describing where one object is in relation to another or determining the best location to place an item.\n\nThe research suggests that spatial reasoning failures are multifaceted, involving algorithmic limitations, architectural design choices, and fundamental challenges in understanding complex spatial relationships.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"534adadd-07b4-405e-96ee-e3395938370a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:47.506Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d2235eb1-6676-46cf-ab75-fc453774236f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fbd0fa43-762b-4a06-b996-3076c036ce6c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a55aa02cbc6f623ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BThcxxuzPjScvHKke2JW9K","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LLM \"as optimizer\" small scale failure scaling combinatorial limitation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Revisiting OPRO: The Limitations of Small-Scale LLMs as Optimizers | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/384212804_Revisiting_OPRO_The_Limitations_of_Small-Scale_LLMs_as_Optimizers\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Optimizing with Large Language Models | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=vIU8LUckb4&noteId=gpH4t72ERS\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling LLM Test-Time Compute Optimally can be More Effective than Scaling Model Parameters\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2408.03314v1\"},{\"title\":\"Are More LLM Calls All You Need? Towards Scaling Laws of Compound Inference Systems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2403.02419v1\"},{\"title\":\"A Systematic Survey on Large Language Models for Evolutionary Optimization: From Modeling to Solving\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.08269v1\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing LLM Inference. Optimization begins where architectures… | by Bijit Ghosh | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@bijit211987/optimizing-llm-inference-f7576d906990\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ai4co/awesome-fm4co: Recent research papers about Foundation Models for Combinatorial Optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ai4co/awesome-fm4co\"},{\"title\":\"Large Language Models as End-to-end Combinatorial Optimization Solvers | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=qr5uMEs6iR\"},{\"title\":\"LLM Inference Optimization Techniques: A Comprehensive Analysis | by Sahin Ahmed(Data Scientist/MLE) | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@sahin.samia/llm-inference-optimization-techniques-a-comprehensive-analysis-1c434e85ba7c\"},{\"title\":\"[2408.03314] Scaling LLM Test-Time Compute Optimally can be More Effective than Scaling Model Parameters\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.03314\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Main Results\n\n**Small-Scale Performance:** LLMs excel at optimizing small-scale problems with limited data and their performance is significantly affected by dimension of problem and values.\n\n**Scaling Limitations:** Existing OPRO-style approaches degrade in large, discrete, and combinatorial domains, where naïve candidate generation and unstructured interaction histories provide weak guidance and limit scalability.\n\n**Combinatorial Challenges:** The combinatorial search space is prohibitively large, and task-specific requirements demand tailored designs when using LLMs for optimization tasks.\n\n**Non-Monotonic Scaling Behavior:** Interestingly, research also found that Voting Inference Systems' performance first increases but then decreases as a function of the number of LLM calls, with this non-monotonicity due to the diversity of query difficulties within a task: more LLM calls lead to higher performance on \"easy\" queries, but lower performance on \"hard\" queries.\n\nThe search results show that while LLMs show promise as optimizers, there are fundamental limitations related to combinatorial complexity, problem dimensionality, and the scalability challenges that arise when moving from small-scale to larger optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9bf9a58b-bc7b-4098-9325-c54245d36025","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:48.129Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fbd0fa43-762b-4a06-b996-3076c036ce6c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9bf9a58b-bc7b-4098-9325-c54245d36025","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a55aa02cbc6f623ac","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01LzCMGK9jXvGzSZqNXaWgSw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have sufficient material. Let me deliver the consolidated research brief.\n\n---\n\n# Reasoning LLM + In-Context Learning 在组合优化上的调研\n\n## 1. ICL for CO 综述（2024-2026）\n\n主流综述把 LLM 用于 CO 分三派：(a) 求解器组件生成（FunSearch、ReEvo），(b) 自动建模（自然语言→MILP/CP），(c) 端到端求解。ACM Computing Surveys 的系统综述（arXiv 2507.03637，筛选 2000+ 论文留 103 篇）明确指出：纯 ICL（给几个 (问题, 解) 例子让模型直接出解）在小规模 TSP/knapsack/CVRP 上能跑，但**在 N>100 后退化严重**。\n\n## 2. Reasoning Models 在 CO 上的实测\n\n- **o1/o3**：o3 在 Codeforces 2727 Elo、AIME 2024 96.7%、FrontierMath 25.2%。但**没有官方 SAT/CSP 标准 benchmark**——SAT 这种结构化任务他们不做主推。\n- **DeepSeek-R1**（Nature 2025, arXiv 2501.12948）：擅长数学/代码/逻辑，但**NP-hard 优化能力欠探索**。NP-Engine（arXiv 2510.16476）专门补这块：10 个 NP-hard 任务、5 个领域，generator-verifier-heuristic 流水线做 RLVR。Qwen2.5-7B-NP 在 NP-Bench 上压过 GPT-4o。\n- **Claude 3.7 Sonnet extended thinking**：AIME 2024 80.0%、GPQA 84.8%、SWE-bench 70.3%。比 R1 略高，但 AIME 落后 o3-mini (87.3%) 和 Grok 3 (93.3%)。\n- **Gemini 2.5 Pro Deep Think**（I/O 2025）：USAMO 高分、AIME 2024/2025 92.0%/86.7%，有 thinking budget 显式控制 token 数。\n- **关键 takeaway**：reasoning model 在**数学证明、代码竞赛**上强；在**大规模空间布局/2D packing**上反而弱。FloorplanQA（arXiv 2507.07644）和 LLaVA controlled study（arXiv 2603.12545）表明：模型经常把\"边界接触\"误判为\"碰撞\"，对 rectangle orientation 搜索不全。\n\n## 3. LLM as Optimizer (OPRO)\n\nDeepMind OPRO 论文（arXiv 2309.03409）：迭代把\"历史 (解, 分数)\"塞 prompt 让 LLM 出新解。在 GSM8K prompt 上 +8%、Big-Bench Hard +50%；但 TSP 只在小规模有效，且后续 \"Revisiting OPRO\" 论文表明**小模型当 optimizer 几乎不工作**，OPRO 在大规模离散组合域 degrade 严重，需要\"结构化交互历史\"才能 scale。\n\n## 4. CoT + 优化决策\n\n代表作 **OLP（Optimizable LLM Planning, OpenReview QxioUQeZO9）**：把 plan 排序当 branch-and-bound，给每个候选估上下界，LLM 输出比较反馈。这跟 FunSearch 风格的\"演化代码\"是两条路：FunSearch 演化的是程序（可重用、可审计），CoT 排序是单点决策（贵但即时）。\n\n## 5. 我们 candidate ranking 任务的可行性\n\n把 frontier + 历史 attempt 序列 + 当前候选列表丢给 reasoning LLM，让它输出 top-k 排序——技术上完全可行。Prompt 模板：\n```\nGoal: max_lex(area, min_side), grid 70x70\nPrevious attempts (top 20): [(rect=18x14, area=252, status=PROVEN), ...]\nCurrent frontier (10 candidates): [(rect=20x12, ...), ...]\nOutput: ranked list with brief reasoning per candidate\n```\n**成本估算**：每候选 ~3-8K reasoning tokens。o3 价格 $2/M in、$8/M out（reasoning token 按 output 计费，且实际可能 3-10× 标价）；o4-mini $1.10/$4.40/M。粗算每候选 $0.05–0.30，每个 wave 200 候选 = $10–60，168h campaign 几十次 wave 累计**几百到上千美元级**。Claude 4 extended thinking 同量级、Gemini 2.5 Pro 含 thinking budget 控制相对便宜。\n\n## 6. 适合 reasoning model 的子问题\n\n合适：(a) **binding 子问题**（小、离散、强结构），(b) **infeasibility classification**（UNKNOWN/UNPROVEN 的语义判读），(c) **tuning 实验解释**。不合适：master 模型 placement、routing flow——这些 70×70 规模、空间连续，LLM 空间推理短板（参 §2）会爆。\n\n## 7. Tool use / Code interpreter\n\no3-mini cookbook 已支持 dynamic tool generation；LLM 可以**自己写 OR-Tools 子模型代码并跑**。但对我们这种已经有成熟 CP-SAT 主模型的项目，更合理的是 LLM **建议 BranchPriority/搜索顺序**（参 arXiv 2508.08147 power system 框架，用 GNN 打分映射到 Gurobi BranchPriority），不是让它自己重写求解器。CP-SAT 的 user propagator 接口可以接收 LLM 给的\"建议变量赋值顺序\"作为软 hint。\n\n## 8. AlphaProof → CO\n\nAlphaProof（Nature 2025, arXiv s41586-025-09833-y）IMO 银牌，但 **combinatorics auto-formalization 只有 33.3% pass@1**（algebra 81.3%、number theory 76.9%）。Lean 形式化对我们 70×70 几何 + 流约束**实际不可行**：状态空间太大、形式化成本远高于直接用 CP-SAT。结论：AlphaProof 路线**短期内不适用**。\n\n## 9. 成本/延迟 vs 替代\n\n| 方案 | 单次决策成本 | 延迟 | 可重用性 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Reasoning LLM 排序 | $0.05–0.30/候选 | 10–60s | 无（每次重算） |\n| LightGBM (训好) | ~$0 | <1ms | 高 |\n| FunSearch 演化代码 | 训练几百美元，跑零成本 | 离线 | 极高 |\n\n**结论**：reasoning LLM 适合**验证阶段/低频决策**，不适合**热路径**。\n\n## 10. AI 安全合同对齐\n\n我们的 contract（CLAUDE.md）：AI 只能 order_only / classify / explain / hint。reasoning LLM 输出**完全符合 hint 类**——它给排序，CP-SAT 该证明的还得证明，证明语义不变。Audit 方案：把每次 LLM 调用的 (prompt hash, response, 采纳与否, 实际结果) 写 JSONL log，与 checkpoint 解耦。**不允许**写 data/checkpoints/、不允许触发 final preflight。\n\n---\n\n## 本项目 PoC 设计\n\n**目标**：验证\"reasoning LLM 排序候选\"能否减少 wave 内无效尝试。\n\n**S-LLM-1（影子模式，2 周）**：\n- 在 outer_search.py 的 frontier 出口插桩，每个 wave 收集 top-50 候选 + 历史 30 个 attempt\n- 调 Claude 4 extended thinking（中等 thinking budget，单次 ~$0.10）输出排序\n- **不改实际执行顺序**，只 log 到 `data/ai_shadow/llm_ranking/*.jsonl`\n- 离线对比：\"如果按 LLM 排序，是否更快命中 PROVEN 候选\"\n\n**S-LLM-2（A/B 验证，2 周）**：\n- 50% wave 用 LLM 排序、50% 用现有规则，比较 wall-clock 到首个 PROVEN 时间\n- 成功阈值：相对加速 >15%，每 wave 成本 <$5\n\n**S-LLM-3（hybrid hint）**：\n- 把 LLM 选出的 top-3 候选传给 CP-SAT 做 search hint（AddHint），不当硬约束\n- 失败立即 fallback 规则路径\n\n**预算上限**：单 168h campaign LLM 调用 < $200，超出自动停 LLM 仅用 deterministic 路径。所有日志写 D:（活跃项目）。\n\n## Sources\n\n- [LLMs for CO: A Systematic Review (arXiv 2507.03637)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.03637)\n- [LLMs as End-to-end CO Solvers (NeurIPS 2025)](https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/115835)\n- [Awesome FM4CO](https://github.com/ai4co/awesome-fm4co)\n- [Awesome ML4CO](https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co)\n- [DeepSeek-R1 (arXiv 2501.12948)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.12948)\n- [DeepSeek-R1 Nature paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09422-z)\n- [NP-Engine (arXiv 2510.16476)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.16476)\n- [OPRO: Large Language Models as Optimizers (arXiv 2309.03409)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.03409)\n- [OPRO GitHub](https://github.com/google-deepmind/opro)\n- [Revisiting OPRO Limitations](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/384212804_Revisiting_OPRO_The_Limitations_of_Small-Scale_LLMs_as_Optimizers)\n- [OPT-Engine: Benchmarking LLMs in Optimization (arXiv 2601.19924)](https://arxiv.org/html/2601.19924)\n- [LLMs as Hyper-Heuristics / ReEvo (arXiv 2402.01145)](https://arxiv.org/html/2402.01145v2)\n- [FunSearch Nature paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06924-6)\n- [FunSearch DeepMind blog](https://deepmind.google/blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/)\n- [AlphaProof Nature 2025](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y)\n- [AlphaProof DeepMind blog](https://deepmind.google/blog/ai-solves-imo-problems-at-silver-medal-level/)\n- [Optimizable LLM Planning OLP](https://openreview.net/pdf?id=QxioUQeZO9)\n- [Claude 3.7 Sonnet announcement](https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-7-sonnet)\n- [Claude visible extended thinking](https://www.anthropic.com/news/visible-extended-thinking)\n- [Gemini 2.5 thinking model](https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/gemini-model-thinking-updates-march-2025/)\n- [Gemini Deep Think TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2025/05/20/deep-think-boosts-the-performance-of-googles-flagship-google-gemini-ai-model/)\n- [OpenAI o3 benchmarks (Helicone)](https://www.helicone.ai/blog/openai-o3)\n- [o3 pricing analysis](https://tokenmix.ai/blog/openai-o3-pricing)\n- [o4-mini pricing](https://www.burnwise.io/ai-pricing/model/o4-mini)\n- [Artificial Analysis: o1](https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/o1)\n- [Artificial Analysis: Gemini 2.5 Pro](https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/gemini-2-5-pro)\n- [LLM-Assisted Power System Optimization (arXiv 2508.08147)](https://arxiv.org/html/2508.08147)\n- [3D Packing case study (arXiv 2509.02297)](https://arxiv.org/html/2509.02297v1)\n- [FloorplanQA spatial reasoning benchmark](https://arxiv.org/html/2507.07644)\n- [Spatial reasoning controlled study (arXiv 2603.12545)](https://arxiv.org/html/2603.12545)\n- [Code Interpreter Tool for LLM Agents (OpenAI cookbook)](https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/examples/object_oriented_agentic_approach/secure_code_interpreter_tool_for_llm_agents)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2829,"cache_read_input_tokens":44135,"output_tokens":4525,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2829},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4525,"cache_read_inp